# Configuration in the development environment (docs/design/25-config-and-secrets.md).
# `.env` sets APP_GREETING, APP_API_TOKEN, APP_MODE, APP_TAGS and
# APP_SIGNING_KEY_FILE (a path relative to the project root); every other
# field takes its default.

### values come from .env, then the defaults
GET /config/all
>>> 200
~ greeting=howdy
~ retries=3
~ timeout=90s

### an enum value is read by its case name
GET /config/all
>>> 200
~ mode=strict

### a list value is comma-separated with spaces trimmed
GET /config/all
>>> 200
~ tags=3:red|green|blue

### a missing optional field is nil
GET /config/all
>>> 200
~ nickname=nil

### a secret interpolates as Secret(•••)
GET /config/all
>>> 200
~ token=Secret(•••)
~ key=Secret(•••)

### a secret's value never appears in a response that printed it
GET /config/all
>>> 200
!~ tok_e2e_SECRET_7f3a9c
!~ whsec_e2eFILEkey42

### matches compares a candidate with a secret
GET /config/token?candidate=tok_e2e_SECRET_7f3a9c
>>> 200
= match

### a wrong candidate doesn't match
GET /config/token?candidate=tok_e2e_SECRET_7f3a9
>>> 200
= no match

### an empty candidate doesn't match
GET /config/token
>>> 200
= no match

### a NAME_FILE secret is read from the file relative to the project root
GET /config/key?candidate=whsec_e2eFILEkey42
>>> 200
= match

### one trailing line ending is removed from a secret file
GET /config/key?candidate=whsec_e2eFILEkey42%0A
>>> 200
= no match

### a config value reaches a page only through the rpc, with the secret redacted
GET /welcome
>>> 200
~ howdy (token Secret(•••))
!~ tok_e2e_SECRET_7f3a9c

### the page's hydration data holds the loaded text, not the config
GET /welcome
>>> 200
~ "text":"howdy (token Secret(•••))"
!~ APP_API_TOKEN
